1
00:00:02,467 --> 00:00:04,052
KATARA: Water...

2
00:00:04,886 --> 00:00:06,346
Earth...

3
00:00:06,888 --> 00:00:08,515
Fire...

4
00:00:08,973 --> 00:00:10,225
Air.

5
00:00:11,226 --> 00:00:14,646
Long ago, the four nations
lived together in harmony.

6
00:00:15,355 --> 00:00:18,816
Then everything changed
when the Fire Nation attacked.

7
00:00:19,734 --> 00:00:22,570
Only the Avatar,
master of all four elements,

8
00:00:22,654 --> 00:00:23,738
could stop them.

9
00:00:23,821 --> 00:00:25,490
But when the world
needed him most,

10
00:00:25,573 --> 00:00:26,741
he vanished.

11
00:00:27,367 --> 00:00:28,785
100 years passed,

12
00:00:28,868 --> 00:00:31,120
and my brother and I
discovered the new Avatar―

13
00:00:31,371 --> 00:00:32,872
An airbender named Aang.

14
00:00:32,956 --> 00:00:35,083
And although his airbending
skills are great,

15
00:00:35,166 --> 00:00:38,002
he has a lot to learn before
he's ready to save anyone.

16
00:00:38,086 --> 00:00:39,087
AANG: Oof.

17
00:00:39,170 --> 00:00:42,298
But I believe Aang
can save the world.

18
00:00:51,724 --> 00:00:53,476
ZHAO: I discovered a hidden library.

19
00:00:54,018 --> 00:00:56,896
I tore through
scroll after scroll.

20
00:00:59,941 --> 00:01:01,067
TOPH: You did it!

21
00:01:01,359 --> 00:01:02,485
You're an earthbender.

22
00:01:03,069 --> 00:01:06,573
ROKU: Sozin's Comet will return
by the end of the summer.

23
00:01:06,656 --> 00:01:10,410
And Fire Lord Ozai will use
its power to finish the war

24
00:01:10,493 --> 00:01:11,911
once and for all.

25
00:01:12,370 --> 00:01:14,706
You must defeat the Fire Lord

26
00:01:14,789 --> 00:01:16,708
before the comet arrives.

27
00:01:26,509 --> 00:01:27,635
SOKKA: What's out here?

28
00:01:27,885 --> 00:01:30,513
TOPH: A lot, actually.
There's hundreds of little―

29
00:01:30,597 --> 00:01:32,682
Shh! I know you
can see underground,

30
00:01:32,765 --> 00:01:34,434
but don't ruin the surprise.

31
00:01:34,517 --> 00:01:35,810
Just watch.

32
00:01:36,227 --> 00:01:37,228
♪♪
♪♪

33
00:01:37,312 --> 00:01:38,438
♪ Eh ♪

34
00:01:38,521 --> 00:01:39,731
Ha ha! Yeah!

35
00:01:40,106 --> 00:01:41,357
♪♪
♪♪

36
00:01:41,441 --> 00:01:42,442
♪ Eh! ♪

37
00:01:42,525 --> 00:01:44,235
I'm putting
an orchestra together.

38
00:01:44,319 --> 00:01:45,653
Orchestra, huh? Well...

39
00:01:45,737 --> 00:01:47,280
♪ La-di-da ♪

40
00:01:47,572 --> 00:01:49,115
-♪ Laah ♪
-♪ Diih ♪

41
00:01:49,240 --> 00:01:50,241
♪ Daah ♪

42
00:01:52,744 --> 00:01:53,745
♪♪
♪♪

43
00:01:53,828 --> 00:01:54,829
♪ Eh ♪

44
00:01:54,912 --> 00:01:55,955
♪ Eh! ♪

45
00:01:56,039 --> 00:01:57,040
♪ Eh! ♪

46
00:01:57,123 --> 00:01:58,291
♪ Eh ♪

47
00:01:59,292 --> 00:02:00,376
This is great and all,

48
00:02:00,460 --> 00:02:03,046
But don't we have more important things
to worry about?

49
00:02:03,129 --> 00:02:04,380
We should be making plans.

50
00:02:04,714 --> 00:02:06,174
We did make plans.

51
00:02:06,257 --> 00:02:07,884
We're all picking mini-vacations.

52
00:02:08,176 --> 00:02:10,053
There's no time for vacations.

53
00:02:10,345 --> 00:02:12,347
I'm learning the elements
as fast as I can.

54
00:02:12,555 --> 00:02:15,475
I practice hard every day
with Toph and Katara.

55
00:02:15,558 --> 00:02:17,101
I've been training
my arrow off.

56
00:02:17,477 --> 00:02:20,688
Yeah. What's wrong with having a little
fun in our downtime?

57
00:02:20,772 --> 00:02:23,399
Even if you do master all of
the elements, then what?

58
00:02:23,483 --> 00:02:25,693
It's not like we have
a map of the Fire Nation.

59
00:02:25,777 --> 00:02:28,696
Should we just head west
until we reach the Fire Lord's house?

60
00:02:28,780 --> 00:02:31,616
Knock, knock! Hello, Fire Lord!
Anybody home?

61
00:02:31,699 --> 00:02:32,950
I don't think so.

62
00:02:33,034 --> 00:02:35,578
We need some intelligence
if we're gonna win this war.

63
00:02:35,662 --> 00:02:36,663
♪ Laah ♪

64
00:02:36,746 --> 00:02:39,332
Hee hee! All right.
We'll finish our vacations.

65
00:02:39,415 --> 00:02:41,626
And then we'll look
for Sokka's intelligence.

66
00:02:43,127 --> 00:02:44,504
AANG: Your turn, Katara.

67
00:02:44,587 --> 00:02:46,881
Where would you
like to go on your mini-vacation?

68
00:02:46,964 --> 00:02:49,384
How about
the Misty Palms Oasis?

69
00:02:49,467 --> 00:02:50,593
That sounds refreshing.

70
00:02:50,677 --> 00:02:53,596
Oh, yeah, I've been there.
It's a pristine natural ice spring.

71
00:02:53,680 --> 00:02:56,099
And I don't usually
use the word "pristine."

72
00:02:56,182 --> 00:02:58,267
It's one of
nature's wonders.

73
00:02:58,351 --> 00:02:59,852
( SOUNDTRACK MUSIC SLOWS DOWN )

74
00:03:00,395 --> 00:03:03,690
Must have changed
ownership since I was here.

75
00:03:03,773 --> 00:03:05,233
Heh heh.

76
00:03:15,284 --> 00:03:16,452
Ptooey!

77
00:03:18,496 --> 00:03:19,789
( GROWLING )

78
00:03:25,712 --> 00:03:27,255
( SNORING )

79
00:03:27,338 --> 00:03:28,965
One mango, please.

80
00:03:42,895 --> 00:03:44,397
I don't see anything wrong

81
00:03:44,480 --> 00:03:46,691
with having one of those
fruity beverages

82
00:03:46,774 --> 00:03:48,735
while we plan our strategy.

83
00:03:49,819 --> 00:03:50,903
Excuse me.

84
00:03:54,240 --> 00:03:56,159
No worries. I clean up easy.

85
00:03:59,036 --> 00:04:00,413
You're a living relic.

86
00:04:00,496 --> 00:04:01,998
Thanks. I try.

87
00:04:02,081 --> 00:04:05,126
An Air Nomad right front of me.

88
00:04:05,209 --> 00:04:06,919
Professor Zei,
head of anthropology

89
00:04:07,003 --> 00:04:08,671
at Ba Sing Se University.

90
00:04:08,963 --> 00:04:10,089
Tell me...

91
00:04:10,173 --> 00:04:13,134
Which of the air temples
do you hail from?

92
00:04:13,217 --> 00:04:14,343
The Southern Temple.

93
00:04:14,427 --> 00:04:16,763
Oh, splendid! Now, tell me,

94
00:04:16,846 --> 00:04:19,640
what was the primary
agricultural product of your people?

95
00:04:19,724 --> 00:04:23,436
Uh, are fruit pies
an agricultural product?

96
00:04:23,603 --> 00:04:27,064
Oh! Truly fascinating.
That's one for the journal.

97
00:04:27,356 --> 00:04:30,568
SOKKA: So, professor,
you're obviously a well-traveled guy.

98
00:04:30,651 --> 00:04:32,195
Do you have a more
current map?

99
00:04:32,278 --> 00:04:33,780
Ours seems to be
a little dated.

100
00:04:34,363 --> 00:04:35,615
Certainly.

101
00:04:38,367 --> 00:04:40,286
What? No Fire Nation?

102
00:04:40,369 --> 00:04:42,789
Doesn't anybody have
a good map of that place?

103
00:04:43,039 --> 00:04:45,458
KATARA: You've made a lot
of trips into the desert.

104
00:04:45,541 --> 00:04:46,959
ZEI: All in vain, I'm afraid.

105
00:04:47,043 --> 00:04:50,129
I've found lost civilizations
all over the Earth Kingdom,

106
00:04:50,213 --> 00:04:53,800
but I haven't managed to find
the crown jewel―

107
00:04:54,258 --> 00:04:56,511
Wan Shi Tong's library.

108
00:04:56,928 --> 00:05:00,348
You've spent years
walking through the desert to find

109
00:05:00,431 --> 00:05:01,682
some guy's library?

110
00:05:02,016 --> 00:05:05,436
This library is more valuable
than gold, little lady.

111
00:05:05,520 --> 00:05:09,148
It is said to contain a vast collection
of knowledge.

112
00:05:09,232 --> 00:05:10,483
And knowledge...

113
00:05:11,067 --> 00:05:12,276
Is priceless.

114
00:05:12,360 --> 00:05:14,570
( DEADPAN ) Hmm. Sounds like good times.

115
00:05:14,862 --> 00:05:17,281
Oh, it is. According to legend,

116
00:05:17,365 --> 00:05:20,034
It was built by the great knowledge spirit

117
00:05:20,159 --> 00:05:24,330
Wan Shi Tong with the help
of his foxy knowledge seekers.

118
00:05:24,705 --> 00:05:28,084
Oh, so this spirit
has attractive assistants, huh?

119
00:05:28,167 --> 00:05:30,795
I think he means
they look like actual foxes, Sokka.

120
00:05:30,878 --> 00:05:32,171
ZEI: You're both right.

121
00:05:32,255 --> 00:05:33,881
Handsome little creatures.

122
00:05:33,965 --> 00:05:36,092
Wan Shi Tong and his knowledge seekers

123
00:05:36,175 --> 00:05:38,469
collected books from all over the world

124
00:05:38,553 --> 00:05:41,556
and put them on display
for mankind to read

125
00:05:41,639 --> 00:05:43,391
so that we might better ourselves.

126
00:05:43,474 --> 00:05:45,726
If this place has books
from all over the world,

127
00:05:45,810 --> 00:05:48,729
do you think they've got
info on the Fire Nation? A map maybe?

128
00:05:48,813 --> 00:05:49,897
I wouldn't know.

129
00:05:50,022 --> 00:05:52,233
But if such a thing exists,

130
00:05:52,316 --> 00:05:54,819
it's in Wan Shi Tong's library.

131
00:05:56,362 --> 00:05:59,490
Then it's settled. Aang,
I do believe it's my turn.

132
00:05:59,574 --> 00:06:02,577
I'd like to spend my vacation
at the library!

133
00:06:03,786 --> 00:06:07,081
Uh, hey, what about me?
When do I get to pick?

134
00:06:07,164 --> 00:06:09,000
You've got to work
here a little longer

135
00:06:09,083 --> 00:06:11,210
before you're qualified
for vacation time.

136
00:06:11,294 --> 00:06:12,295
Hmph.

137
00:06:12,378 --> 00:06:14,463
Of course, there's the matter
of finding it.

138
00:06:14,547 --> 00:06:16,799
I've made several trips
into the Zi Huang desert

139
00:06:16,883 --> 00:06:18,634
and almost died each time.

140
00:06:18,718 --> 00:06:21,846
I'm afraid that desert's
impossible to cross.

141
00:06:22,847 --> 00:06:25,558
Professor, would you like to see
our sky bison?

142
00:06:25,808 --> 00:06:29,186
A sky bison? You actually have one?!

143
00:06:29,270 --> 00:06:31,439
( GROWLING )

144
00:06:31,522 --> 00:06:34,150
Sandbenders, shoo!
Away from the bison!

145
00:06:55,922 --> 00:06:58,966
Tell me, sky bison,
are you the last of your breed?

146
00:07:00,217 --> 00:07:03,846
Oh, delightful! I only wish
I spoke his tongue.

147
00:07:03,930 --> 00:07:06,807
Oh, the stories this beast could tell.

148
00:07:08,142 --> 00:07:09,268
Shush, chatty monkey.

149
00:07:10,478 --> 00:07:12,063
Wow. It shouldn't be too hard

150
00:07:12,146 --> 00:07:13,814
to find a place like this out here.

151
00:07:18,402 --> 00:07:20,529
Ah! Does this place even exist?

152
00:07:20,613 --> 00:07:22,073
Some say it doesn't.

153
00:07:22,949 --> 00:07:25,618
Shouldn't you have mentioned that before?

154
00:07:25,743 --> 00:07:26,827
Grr!

155
00:07:32,041 --> 00:07:33,459
There it is!

156
00:07:37,964 --> 00:07:40,800
That's what it will sound like
when one of you spots it.

157
00:07:43,010 --> 00:07:44,136
( APPA GROWLING )

158
00:07:45,388 --> 00:07:48,891
It shouldn't be this hard to spot
a giant ornate building from the air.

159
00:07:52,687 --> 00:07:54,355
Down there. What's that?

160
00:07:59,485 --> 00:08:02,113
Forget it. It's obviously not
what we're looking for.

161
00:08:02,446 --> 00:08:04,365
The building in this
drawing is enormous.

162
00:08:13,416 --> 00:08:14,875
What kind of animal is that?

163
00:08:18,254 --> 00:08:20,673
ZEI: I think that was one
of the knowledge seekers.

164
00:08:21,173 --> 00:08:23,009
Oh, we must be close to the library.

165
00:08:23,467 --> 00:08:26,512
No. This is the library. Look!

166
00:08:29,098 --> 00:08:30,266
It's completely buried.

167
00:08:38,607 --> 00:08:40,735
ZEI: The library is buried?!

168
00:08:40,818 --> 00:08:43,529
My life's ambition is now full of sand.

169
00:08:44,113 --> 00:08:46,115
Well, time to start excavating.

170
00:08:49,618 --> 00:08:52,038
Actually, that won't
be necessary.

171
00:08:52,121 --> 00:08:54,331
The inside seems to be completely intact.

172
00:08:54,790 --> 00:08:56,083
And it's huge.

173
00:08:56,167 --> 00:08:58,419
SOKKA: That fox thingy
went in through a window.

174
00:08:58,502 --> 00:09:00,796
I say we climb up there
and give it a look.

175
00:09:00,880 --> 00:09:03,132
I say you guys
go ahead without me.

176
00:09:03,215 --> 00:09:05,051
You've got something
against libraries?

177
00:09:05,134 --> 00:09:06,844
I've held books before.

178
00:09:06,927 --> 00:09:08,846
And I got to tell you,

179
00:09:08,929 --> 00:09:10,890
they don't exactly do it for me.

180
00:09:10,973 --> 00:09:12,850
Oh, right. Sorry.

181
00:09:13,267 --> 00:09:15,770
Let me know if they have
something you can listen to.

182
00:09:20,900 --> 00:09:24,820
Don't worry, buddy. I'm not making you
go underground ever again.

183
00:09:24,904 --> 00:09:26,447
You can stay out here with Toph.

184
00:09:32,745 --> 00:09:33,788
What's up?

185
00:09:41,253 --> 00:09:42,421
( CHATTERS )

186
00:09:43,798 --> 00:09:45,841
ZEI: Oh, it's breathtaking.

187
00:09:46,467 --> 00:09:49,053
The spirit spared no expense
in designing this place.

188
00:09:49,136 --> 00:09:51,263
Look at those beautiful buttresses.

189
00:09:51,347 --> 00:09:52,723
- Hee hee!
- Hee hee!

190
00:09:52,807 --> 00:09:54,100
ZEI: What's funny?

191
00:09:54,183 --> 00:09:56,310
Nothing. We just like architecture.

192
00:09:56,811 --> 00:09:58,229
As do I.

193
00:10:01,148 --> 00:10:02,441
My word!

194
00:10:02,566 --> 00:10:07,446
The exquisite mosaic handiwork
of this tile-rendered avian symbol―

195
00:10:07,988 --> 00:10:10,574
Eh, nice owl.

196
00:10:10,658 --> 00:10:11,826
( RUSTLING )

197
00:10:12,618 --> 00:10:13,953
( CHATTERING )

198
00:10:26,382 --> 00:10:28,884
I know you're
back there.

199
00:10:31,554 --> 00:10:32,555
Hello!

200
00:10:32,638 --> 00:10:34,932
I'm Professor Zei, head of anthropology

201
00:10:35,015 --> 00:10:36,392
at Ba Sing Se University.

202
00:10:37,351 --> 00:10:39,812
You should leave
the way you came

203
00:10:39,895 --> 00:10:43,315
Unless you want
to become a stuffed head of anthropology.

204
00:10:43,399 --> 00:10:44,608
( SPEAKING GIBBERISH )

205
00:10:45,151 --> 00:10:48,279
Are you the spirit who brought
this library to the physical world?

206
00:10:48,362 --> 00:10:53,117
Indeed. I am Wan Shi Tong,
he who knows 10,000 things.

207
00:10:53,492 --> 00:10:55,244
And you are obviously humans,

208
00:10:55,661 --> 00:10:58,581
Which, by the way,
are no longer permitted in my study.

209
00:10:58,664 --> 00:11:00,499
AANG: What do you have against humans?

210
00:11:00,583 --> 00:11:03,752
Hmm. Humans only bother learning things

211
00:11:03,836 --> 00:11:05,546
to get the edge on other humans,

212
00:11:05,963 --> 00:11:09,508
Like that firebender who came
to this place a few years ago,

213
00:11:09,592 --> 00:11:11,927
looking to destroy his enemy.

214
00:11:12,386 --> 00:11:15,431
So who are you trying to destroy?

215
00:11:15,764 --> 00:11:19,977
What? No, no, no destroying.
We're not into that.

216
00:11:20,060 --> 00:11:22,479
WAN SHI TONG: Then why have you come here?

217
00:11:22,897 --> 00:11:26,525
Um, knowledge for knowledge's sake.

218
00:11:27,443 --> 00:11:30,905
If you're going to lie
to an all-knowing spirit being,

219
00:11:30,988 --> 00:11:33,115
you should at least
put some effort into it.

220
00:11:33,199 --> 00:11:35,534
I'm not lying! I'm here with the Avatar,

221
00:11:35,618 --> 00:11:38,746
And he's the bridge between our worlds.
He'll vouch for me.

222
00:11:39,121 --> 00:11:40,122
Ow!

223
00:11:40,581 --> 00:11:43,334
Uh, yeah. I'll vouch.

224
00:11:43,667 --> 00:11:46,670
We will not abuse the knowledge
in your library, good spirit.

225
00:11:46,754 --> 00:11:48,214
You have my word.

226
00:11:48,297 --> 00:11:53,802
Hmm. Very well.
I'll let you peruse my vast collection

227
00:11:53,886 --> 00:11:55,471
on one condition―

228
00:11:55,846 --> 00:11:57,765
To prove your worth as scholars,

229
00:11:57,848 --> 00:12:01,185
you have to contribute
some worthwhile knowledge.

230
00:12:02,102 --> 00:12:05,564
Please accept this tome
as a donation to your library.

231
00:12:06,065 --> 00:12:08,776
First edition. Very nice.

232
00:12:12,613 --> 00:12:14,615
I have an authentic waterbending scroll.

233
00:12:15,074 --> 00:12:18,827
Oh, these illustrations are quite stylish.

234
00:12:20,788 --> 00:12:22,623
Uh, oh! I know.

235
00:12:23,832 --> 00:12:24,833
Ha!

236
00:12:25,209 --> 00:12:27,086
I suppose that counts.

237
00:12:29,004 --> 00:12:31,840
Oh, great spirit, check this out.

238
00:12:32,132 --> 00:12:33,509
Ta-da!

239
00:12:34,927 --> 00:12:36,053
It's a special knot.

240
00:12:36,136 --> 00:12:37,346
That counts as knowledge.

241
00:12:38,222 --> 00:12:40,349
You're not very bright, are you?

242
00:12:42,518 --> 00:12:44,186
Enjoy the library.

243
00:12:51,360 --> 00:12:53,153
Bright enough to fool you.

244
00:12:56,865 --> 00:13:00,035
So, do you like flying?

245
00:13:02,329 --> 00:13:05,541
Of course, I'm more comfortable
on the ground where I can see.

246
00:13:05,624 --> 00:13:08,252
Well, I don't see the way you do.

247
00:13:08,627 --> 00:13:11,380
I feel the vibrations in the ground
with my feet.

248
00:13:11,755 --> 00:13:14,591
But this sand is
so loose and shifty,

249
00:13:14,675 --> 00:13:16,719
It makes everything look fuzzy.

250
00:13:16,802 --> 00:13:18,262
( GROWLS )

251
00:13:18,345 --> 00:13:20,514
Not that there's
anything wrong with fuzzy.

252
00:13:31,525 --> 00:13:33,610
Hey! Look at these
weird lion-turtle things.

253
00:13:34,903 --> 00:13:36,363
Ah, I've seen weirder.

254
00:13:36,447 --> 00:13:39,575
Aang, did you know in a past life,
you were left-handed?

255
00:13:39,658 --> 00:13:41,452
I always knew I was special.

256
00:13:51,503 --> 00:13:54,923
"The darkest day in Fire Nation history."

257
00:13:55,257 --> 00:13:56,592
It's got a date at the top,

258
00:13:56,675 --> 00:13:58,427
but it doesn't say anything else.

259
00:14:04,975 --> 00:14:06,810
Sokka, where are you going?

260
00:14:06,894 --> 00:14:10,147
I want to know what happened
to the Fire Nation on their darkest day.

261
00:14:10,230 --> 00:14:11,398
This could be promising.

262
00:14:13,484 --> 00:14:16,403
The information on the Fire Nation
should be right up here.

263
00:14:19,323 --> 00:14:20,449
AANG: Firebenders.

264
00:14:20,532 --> 00:14:23,744
KATARA: They destroyed everything
having to do with the Fire Nation.

265
00:14:24,286 --> 00:14:25,746
That's so unfair!

266
00:14:25,829 --> 00:14:28,457
Just when I think
I'm one step ahead of the Fire Nation,

267
00:14:28,540 --> 00:14:31,001
it turns out they beat us here
a long time ago.

268
00:14:31,752 --> 00:14:34,380
I need to know what happened
on the darkest day.

269
00:14:34,463 --> 00:14:35,964
( WHIMPERING )

270
00:14:36,715 --> 00:14:39,676
Hello, little weird fox guy.

271
00:14:42,137 --> 00:14:44,223
ZEI: It seems it's trying to assist you.

272
00:14:44,890 --> 00:14:48,268
Um, sure. I guess I'll follow you.

273
00:15:15,671 --> 00:15:19,633
This room is a true marvel,
a mechanical wonder.

274
00:15:19,716 --> 00:15:22,928
It's a planetarium
that shows the heavens moving.

275
00:15:25,848 --> 00:15:28,684
SOKKA: This is beautiful,
but how is it helpful?

276
00:15:29,226 --> 00:15:32,104
Maybe these dials
represent dates and times.

277
00:15:32,187 --> 00:15:35,065
Sokka, try entering that date
from that parchment you took.

278
00:15:35,441 --> 00:15:40,279
Shh! Katara, not in front of the fox.
He's with the owl.

279
00:15:40,529 --> 00:15:41,530
( WHIMPERS )

280
00:15:59,465 --> 00:16:01,925
Wow! I got to hand it to you, Sokka,

281
00:16:02,009 --> 00:16:04,553
You picked
the best mini-vacation for sure.

282
00:16:08,849 --> 00:16:10,934
KATARA: Hey, wait.
What happened to the sun?

283
00:16:11,852 --> 00:16:13,979
Great. You must have broken it.

284
00:16:14,354 --> 00:16:15,981
It's not broken.

285
00:16:17,316 --> 00:16:20,861
The sun is behind the moon.
It's a solar eclipse.

286
00:16:21,236 --> 00:16:24,281
It's literally the darkest day
in Fire Nation history.

287
00:16:24,364 --> 00:16:26,825
Now I get it.
Something awful happened on that day.

288
00:16:26,909 --> 00:16:28,702
I don't know what, but I do know why.

289
00:16:29,077 --> 00:16:32,831
Firebenders lose their bending
during a solar eclipse.

290
00:16:32,915 --> 00:16:33,957
Sorry.

291
00:16:34,041 --> 00:16:35,042
That makes sense.

292
00:16:35,125 --> 00:16:37,794
I mean, think of what the lunar eclipse
at the North Pole

293
00:16:37,878 --> 00:16:39,213
did to the waterbenders.

294
00:16:39,296 --> 00:16:40,339
This is huge.

295
00:16:40,422 --> 00:16:41,423
( FOX WHIMPERS )

296
00:16:43,842 --> 00:16:45,135
Fine. You earned it.

297
00:16:47,429 --> 00:16:50,557
We've got to get this information
to the Earth King at Ba Sing Se.

298
00:16:50,641 --> 00:16:52,184
We'll wait for the next eclipse.

299
00:16:52,267 --> 00:16:55,270
Then we'll invade the Fire Nation
when they're totally helpless.

300
00:16:55,354 --> 00:16:57,022
The Fire Lord is going down!

301
00:16:57,981 --> 00:17:00,317
Mortals are so predictable

302
00:17:00,776 --> 00:17:02,819
and such terrible liars.

303
00:17:03,529 --> 00:17:04,530
( SOKKA GULPS )

304
00:17:09,159 --> 00:17:11,036
You betrayed my trust.

305
00:17:11,411 --> 00:17:14,289
From the beginning,
you intended to misuse this knowledge

306
00:17:14,373 --> 00:17:15,791
for evil purposes.

307
00:17:16,166 --> 00:17:19,545
You don't understand.
If anyone's evil, it's the Fire Nation.

308
00:17:19,628 --> 00:17:21,463
You saw what they did to your library.

309
00:17:21,547 --> 00:17:23,423
They're destructive and dangerous.

310
00:17:23,507 --> 00:17:25,259
We need this information.

311
00:17:25,676 --> 00:17:29,263
You think you're the first person
to believe their war was justified?

312
00:17:29,388 --> 00:17:31,765
Countless others before
you have come here,

313
00:17:31,848 --> 00:17:34,935
seeking weapons
or weaknesses or battle strategies.

314
00:17:35,185 --> 00:17:38,063
We had no choice.
Please. We're just desperate to protect

315
00:17:38,146 --> 00:17:39,398
the people we love.

316
00:17:39,731 --> 00:17:43,569
And now I am going
to protect what I love.

317
00:17:47,072 --> 00:17:48,448
AANG: What are you doing?

318
00:17:48,865 --> 00:17:54,162
I'm taking my knowledge back.
No one will ever abuse it again.

319
00:17:54,413 --> 00:17:57,040
He's sinking the building.
We've got to get out of here!

320
00:17:57,249 --> 00:18:01,587
I'm afraid I can't allow that.
You already know too much.

321
00:18:01,962 --> 00:18:03,005
- Aah!
- Aah!

322
00:18:03,755 --> 00:18:05,215
( KIDS SCREAMING )

323
00:18:10,387 --> 00:18:11,847
( GROWLS )

324
00:18:12,180 --> 00:18:14,850
I already told you.
I don't want to snuggle.

325
00:18:19,563 --> 00:18:22,774
Library's sinking.
Library's sinking!

326
00:18:23,483 --> 00:18:25,027
Hyah!

327
00:18:33,452 --> 00:18:34,536
( YELLS )

328
00:18:51,094 --> 00:18:52,304
Aah!

329
00:18:53,013 --> 00:18:55,098
Great knowledge spirit, I beg you,

330
00:18:55,182 --> 00:18:59,311
do not destroy your vast collection
of priceless tomes.

331
00:19:00,854 --> 00:19:02,356
Aah!

332
00:19:10,656 --> 00:19:12,658
We've got to get back to the surface.

333
00:19:14,743 --> 00:19:16,078
Sokka, let's go.

334
00:19:16,411 --> 00:19:19,331
But we still don't know
when the next eclipse is gonna happen.

335
00:19:19,414 --> 00:19:21,208
Don't be stupid.
We'll find out later.

336
00:19:21,291 --> 00:19:23,418
No, we won't.
If we leave this place,

337
00:19:23,543 --> 00:19:25,087
we'll never get the information.

338
00:19:25,170 --> 00:19:27,756
Aang, come with me
to the planetarium. I need cover.

339
00:19:28,090 --> 00:19:29,925
Katara, take Momo and get out of here.

340
00:19:30,008 --> 00:19:31,009
But―

341
00:19:31,134 --> 00:19:32,135
SOKKA: Go!

342
00:19:32,928 --> 00:19:33,929
Hurry, Sokka!

343
00:19:41,395 --> 00:19:42,604
( BREATHING HEAVILY )

344
00:19:48,694 --> 00:19:50,278
What is it now?

345
00:19:58,829 --> 00:19:59,996
Who is there?

346
00:20:07,462 --> 00:20:08,880
AANG: Why are we doing this?

347
00:20:08,964 --> 00:20:11,967
Because if this calendar can tell us
about eclipses in the past,

348
00:20:12,050 --> 00:20:14,511
then maybe it can project
when the next one will be.

349
00:20:14,594 --> 00:20:16,596
You can't possibly
check every single date.

350
00:20:16,680 --> 00:20:18,765
I don't have to.
We just need to check

351
00:20:18,890 --> 00:20:20,892
every date before Sozin's Comet arrives,

352
00:20:20,976 --> 00:20:24,521
because after that,
well, try not to think about that.

353
00:20:44,583 --> 00:20:45,709
Come on, eclipse!

354
00:20:49,379 --> 00:20:51,381
SOKKA: That's it― The solar eclipse.

355
00:20:51,465 --> 00:20:53,175
It's just a few months away.

356
00:20:54,926 --> 00:20:57,179
Got it! Now let's get to Ba Sing Se.

357
00:21:15,155 --> 00:21:17,407
Don't make me put this down.

358
00:21:27,459 --> 00:21:29,795
No! Stop sinking!

359
00:21:34,257 --> 00:21:35,342
No!

360
00:21:36,593 --> 00:21:37,886
I'm sorry, Appa.

361
00:21:42,098 --> 00:21:43,850
-( CHATTERING )
-( SCREECHING )

362
00:21:56,863 --> 00:22:00,325
At least I'll have one specimen
to add to my collection.

363
00:22:00,408 --> 00:22:01,785
Aah!

364
00:22:11,086 --> 00:22:13,797
Your waterbending
won't do you much good here.

365
00:22:14,297 --> 00:22:17,467
I've studied northern water style,
southern water style,

366
00:22:17,551 --> 00:22:20,136
even foggy swamp style.

367
00:22:21,304 --> 00:22:23,932
Hyah!

368
00:22:25,976 --> 00:22:28,854
That's called Sokka style. Learn it.

369
00:22:35,026 --> 00:22:37,529
Wait! Professor, let's go.

370
00:22:37,946 --> 00:22:40,407
I'm not leaving. I can't.

371
00:22:40,490 --> 00:22:43,118
I've spent too long
trying to find this place.

372
00:22:43,368 --> 00:22:45,370
There's not
another collection of knowledge

373
00:22:45,453 --> 00:22:46,580
like this on earth.

374
00:22:47,998 --> 00:22:50,458
I could spend an eternity in here.

375
00:22:50,917 --> 00:22:51,960
Just go!

376
00:22:52,043 --> 00:22:54,754
( WAN SHI TONG SCREECHES )

377
00:22:55,630 --> 00:22:56,673
( KIDS SCREAMING )

378
00:23:20,071 --> 00:23:22,741
We got it.
There's a solar eclipse coming.

379
00:23:22,824 --> 00:23:24,659
The Fire Nation's in trouble now.

380
00:23:27,621 --> 00:23:29,289
Where's Appa?
